Dear Hextar Chemicals team,

I am writing on behalf of Phyto Beht, a crop protection company registering and distributing plant protection products in Morocco.

We came across Hextar through your product registrations in Malaysia and Brazil, and we understand that your Port Klang site supplies customers in many export markets. We are expanding our portfolio and are looking for a reliable manufacturer of the following active ingredients, as technical grade and/or formulated products: Pyraclostrobin, Deltamethrin, Captan, Cymoxanil and Tebuconazole.

Could you kindly share:
- your product catalogue and the technical specifications (minimum purity, relevant impurities) for these molecules;
- the manufacturing site(s) and your existing registrations, in particular in OECD countries;
- for pyraclostrobin, the crystalline form of your technical material and your position regarding the remaining crystal-form patents;
- the availability of a technical dossier (5-batch analysis, GLP studies, letter of access) to support a registration with ONSSA, the Moroccan authority;
- indicative prices, MOQ, lead times and Incoterms;
- COA, SDS and TDS samples.

We would be glad to schedule a short call to discuss a possible long-term cooperation.

Best regards,
Abderrahmane Chraibi
Agricultural Engineer
Phyto Beht — Morocco
chraibi.agro@gmail.com

Dear Nufarm team,

I am writing on behalf of Phyto Beht, a crop protection company registering and distributing plant protection products in Morocco.

We understand that Nufarm covers North Africa from its office in Tunisia, and that your fluazinam source has already passed an equivalence assessment in France. We are expanding our fungicide range and are looking for a reliable supplier of the following active ingredients, as technical grade and/or formulated products: Prothioconazole, Tebuconazole, Fluazinam, Copper hydroxide and Copper sulphate.

Could you kindly share:
- your product catalogue and the technical specifications (minimum purity, relevant impurities) for these molecules;
- the manufacturing site(s) and your existing registrations, in particular in OECD countries;
- for prothioconazole, the solo and mixture products you can offer, given the mixture patents still in force in some markets;
- the availability of a technical dossier (5-batch analysis, GLP studies, letter of access) to support a registration with ONSSA, the Moroccan authority;
- indicative prices, MOQ, lead times and Incoterms;
- COA, SDS and TDS samples.

We would be glad to schedule a short call, or to meet your North Africa team, to discuss a possible long-term cooperation.

Best regards,
Abderrahmane Chraibi
Agricultural Engineer
Phyto Beht — Morocco
chraibi.agro@gmail.com

Dear Fengshan Group team,

I am writing on behalf of Phyto Beht, a crop protection company registering and distributing plant protection products in Morocco.

We noted that your subsidiary Jiangsu Fengshan Biochemical Technology holds Chinese technical registrations for cyantraniliprole, fluopyram and fluxapyroxad, and that your Dafeng sites are listed with the US EPA. We are looking for a reliable manufacturer of the following active ingredients, as technical grade and/or formulated products: Cyantraniliprole, Fluopyram, Fluxapyroxad, Clodinafop-propargyl and Chlorantraniliprole.

Could you kindly share:
- your product catalogue and the technical specifications (minimum purity, relevant impurities) for these molecules;
- the manufacturing site(s) and your existing registrations, in particular in OECD countries;
- your freedom-to-operate position for export to Morocco on cyantraniliprole, fluopyram and fluxapyroxad (remaining compound, process or mixture patents);
- the availability of a technical dossier (5-batch analysis, GLP studies, letter of access) to support a registration with ONSSA, the Moroccan authority;
- indicative prices, MOQ, lead times and Incoterms;
- COA, SDS and TDS samples.

We would be glad to schedule a short call to discuss a possible long-term cooperation.

Best regards,
Abderrahmane Chraibi
Agricultural Engineer
Phyto Beht — Morocco
chraibi.agro@gmail.com
